120:- **NEARS-3144** (High, AUD-WF-05) — the PO def grants Bash and forbids no git-level restore; a PO ran `git checkout HEAD -- tasks/.atlassian-sync.json` to undo its own JSON round-trip, which restores the last COMMIT and erases every other session's uncommitted rows (latent Critical; the window happened to be clean). (.claude/agents/nears-product-owner.md lines 11, 100, 111; tasks/runs/NEARS-3124.json phases["1"]
134:Shared-ledger rules (`tasks/.atlassian-sync.json` is routinely dirty with other sessions' rows):
136:- Stage your own hunks only — `git apply --cached` of your own entries, or `git add tasks/.atlassian-sync.json` when every dirty row is yours; "never `git add -A`"; never stage another run's entries to get your own committed. (.claude/commands/new-task.md §[9b] Save the work item 6; .claude/commands/run-sprint.md §[4] RUN — batch by batch)

